  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal refrigerator has a freezer at a temperature of $13^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The coefficient of performance of the engine is $5 .$ The temperature of the air (to which heat is rejected) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wMyic",
      "text": "$320^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5EHi2",
      "text": "$39^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "uGRXH",
      "text": "$325 \\mathrm{~K}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FZSZ6",
      "text": "$325^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{T}_{2}=273-13=260$,\n$$\n\\mathrm{K}=\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{2}}{\\mathrm{~T}_{1}-\\mathrm{T}_{2}} ; \\quad 5=\\frac{260}{\\mathrm{~T}_{1}-260}\n$$\nor $\\mathrm{T}_{1}-260=52 ; \\quad \\mathrm{T}_{1}=312 \\mathrm{~K}$\n$\\mathrm{T}_{2}=312-273=39^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$",
    "image": null
